  "observations": [
    "Visual review found synthesized distortions in MI-GAN output while authored optical effects were disabled. GPU and WASM outputs differ by at most one byte per RGB channel for the checked landscape photo.",
    "For mixed_5b channel 120, 5/15/30 independent Dream steps increasingly cover the same scene with repeating cellular texture; this is not evidence of generating new spatial areas.",
    "Two rounds of view-conditioned outpainting invent surroundings but visibly lose detail and the original marmot. Mean horizontal edge difference drops from about 7.70 to 4.41 to 2.38 bytes per channel; this is a diagnostic of detail change, not an aesthetic score.",
    "The small Hello photo gave a visually coherent first outpaint in this sample. The protected text remains in the original image; generated regions were not subjected to OCR.",
    "High-strength Dream views show stretched patterns near the poles. Projection artifacts must be distinguished from model-generated content."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Three photo examples, one Inception target, one hardware configuration, and one photo checked across MI-GAN backends.",
    "No continuous forward-motion illusion or runtime background-generation frame rate has been tested.",
    "Depth and neural relief are disabled in the visual comparisons; no trained depth inference was needed for these tests.",
    "The view-conditioned outpainting chain is a reanchoring experiment, not a reconstructed or persistent 3D world.",
    "Original photos and generated images remain in ignored local test-results; the runner, settings, and measurements are versioned."
  ],
